llama.cpp / ggml - https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

The pre-tokenizer split regex patterns in gmlx/load/tokenizer.py are
transcribed from llama.cpp's tokenizer (llama-vocab.cpp), and the GGUF
metadata/quantization-type conventions follow ggml's reference
implementation. The Muse Glimmer vision tower in
gmlx/models/muse_glimmer/vlm_model.py is ported from llama.cpp's
clip_graph_muse_glimmer and the host-side index math in tools/mtmd/clip.cpp,
and its projector constants and tensor remap in gmlx/load/vlm.py follow
clip.cpp. The Kimi-K3 chat-template fixture
tests/fixtures/kimi_k3_template.jinja comes from llama.cpp PR #26185.
The block output that gmlx capture records in gmlx/tune/capture.py
follows the l_out tensor that tools/cvector-generator reads, and the
stream mean of a hyper-connection residual follows hc_stream_mean.
The LFM3 text model in gmlx/models/lfm3/model.py is ported from
src/models/lfm3.cpp and src/models/lfm-base.cpp at commit e8df20d23, and
the LFM3 speech decoders and reply loop in gmlx/models/lfm3/speech.py and
gmlx/models/lfm3/speak.py from tools/mtmd/models/lfm3a-gen.cpp and
tools/mtmd/mtmd-helper-gen.cpp. Liquid AI contributed these files to
llama.cpp. The LFM3 encoders in gmlx/models/lfm3/audio.py and
gmlx/models/lfm3/vision.py are checked against tools/mtmd/models/lfm3a.cpp
and tools/mtmd/models/lfm3vl.cpp, and their tensor remap in
gmlx/load/vlm.py follows gguf-py's tensor mapping.
